  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_037, acc=0.5420) uses scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. Multiprofile with avgpool and weighted fusion is clearly superior (config_019 vs 009: +0.10; weighted vs concat: +0.013; avgpool vs transformer: +0.03 at 1/4 the cost). The image encoder upgrade (resnet50→ViT) gave +0.017. The remaining major untested variable in this best architecture is the RNA encoder: scvi_n200 has not been paired with ViT+avgpool+weighted. This experiment tests whether scvi_n200 (a variational encoder) can match or exceed scgpt in the strongest multimodal setup, potentially capturing complementary cell-state information. It is the best use of experiment 6 because it directly probes the highest-leverage untested axis (RNA encoder) within the confirmed best architecture, with expected cost comparable to config_037 (~3 GPU hours, since the heavy components—ViT and multiprofile avgpool—remain the same). A positive result would open a new exploitation direction for the remaining 3 experiments; a negative result confirms scgpt as the optimal RNA encoder and narrows the search space."
}

